    <h2>Outbuildings and long runs</h2>
    <p>Power to a detached shop or barn means a buried feeder sized for the distance, a subpanel and proper grounding at the building. We size the wire for the voltage drop, not just the breaker, so tools start without dimming the lights.</p>
    <h2>Farmhouses and additions</h2>
    <p>Many Oakdale farmhouses have been added to over a century, each addition wired by whoever was around at the time. An inspection usually finds a mix of eras behind the walls, and a plan to bring it all onto one safe system.</p>
    <h2>Further out, still on call</h2>
    <p>At about twenty-five minutes from Springfield, Oakdale is well inside our emergency area. Night and weekend calls get the same answer as in town.</p>
</AreaPage>
